          "published_at": "2026-10-25T19:09:31.236Z",
          "url": "https://x.com/HamelHusain/status/2114434195854684330",
          "topic": "Benchmark quality and evaluation practice",
          "text": "I've been looking into public benchmarks and am astounded by the poor quality vs. how much we rely on them as an industry.  \n\n@xeophon pointed me to this excellent site epoch.ai/benchmarks/ which is an independent third party which scrutinizes benchmarks and \"looks at the data\" 💪\n\nFor example, here are some popular benchmarks we all rely on.   Before trusting a benchmark its worth running them and inspecting examples the grader failed carefully, to get a sense of the quality.\n\nI'm continuing to look more into this, and will write something up eventually once I've collected more data, but I think this is an important subject.",
